# STIG CD16-00-009200: Security-relevant software updates to PostgreSQL must be ins
# STIG ID: V-261936 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `pg16-cd16-00-009200-security-update-timely-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `pg16`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG CD16-00-009200: Security-relevant software updates to PostgreSQL must be installed within the ti`
    description `Security-relevant software updates to PostgreSQL must be installed within the time period directed by an authoritative source (e.g., IAVM, CTOs, DTMs, and STIGs).`
    author `example-security`
    tags `pg16,stig,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:CD16-00-009200,NIST-800-53:SI-2`
    control_objective `SI-2`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `dba`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `PostgreSQL16:localhost:pg-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for CD16-00-009200.`

    component_id `comp-pg16-db`

    impl_SI_2 `This control is validated by checking the required PostgreSQL configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT pg_param
        parameter `shared_preload_libraries`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE param_state
        found boolean = true
        value string contains `pgaudit`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN pg_config_param
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF param_state
            OBJECT_REF pg_param
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
